Alerting: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines alert engine policy, severity levels, conditions,
  and project-specific alert configuration.

SeverityLevels:
  INFO:
    - Informational only
    - No action required
  WARNING:
    - Potential issue
    - Monitor closely
  MINOR:
    - Issue affecting non-critical path
    - Action during business hours
  MAJOR:
    - Issue affecting core functionality
    - Immediate action required
  CRITICAL:
    - System down or data loss
    - Page on-call immediately

AlertCondition:
  Format:
    Metric: <metric_name>
    Condition: > | < | == | != | >= | <=
    Threshold: <value>
    Duration: <time_window>
    AND/OR: <additional_conditions>

Examples:
  Error rate > 5% for 5 minutes
  p95 latency > 500ms AND traffic > baseline
  DB connection pool > 90% for 2 minutes

ProjectContextualSeverity:
  Payment:
    refund_failure → CRITICAL
    auth_failure → MAJOR
  Internal:
    UI latency > 1s → WARNING
    report_generation_slow → MINOR

AlertFatigue:
  - Alerts MUST have clear actionability
  - No "CPU > 90%" without context
  - Group related alerts
  - Suppress during maintenance windows

CrossLayer:
  Security: Security alerts feed into incident engine
  Incident: Alerts trigger incident lifecycle when confirmed
  Operations: Alert routing to on-call

State: +
  